A||||6||Silver88GT||How do you know if you need new bushings?||||5||
Z||000000||Silver88GT||12-23-2001||12:03 AM||||This winter I want to replace shocks and struts.  Not sure, but I think it still has the originals.  Not a real big deal since I just turned 70,000.  <P>Anyway, while I was messing with the suspension and getting an alignment, I thought I'd do the bushings too if they needed it.  I know poly will improve handling and all, but I really don't want to mess with this unless I need to.  Unfortunately, I am in that in-between position where I don't have the money to have someone else do it and don't have the time to do it myself.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  Otherwise, I'd go all out and do it right.<P>So, is there a way to tell if the bushings are bad?  I have no reason to believe that they are bad, but also don't have a good point of comparison.<P>Thanks for your input.<P>------------------<BR>Silver88GT (Wingless)||||reg||5
Z||000001||4BanGinFun||12-23-2001||05:45 PM||||one way is if your handling has become poor and if it is squeeky (the rubber is dried out) <P><BR>have fun  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>------------------<BR>85 se 2m4 5spd white<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.stopstart.fsnet.co.uk/flags/canada.gif"> <BR>www.angelfire.com/super/camaro0/||||reg||1
Z||000002||Posthumane||12-23-2001||10:56 PM||||If your wheel falls off along with the control arms and brake rotor.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>I thought only the poly bushings squeaked when they dried up, not rubber...?||||reg||1
Z||000003||Tigger||12-24-2001||07:15 AM||||If your wheel falls off?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif"><P>No, take the wheel off and take a look at the bushings.  You can tell by the ends, if they are heavily cracked, possibly some rubber missing when they are bad.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Posthumane||12-24-2001||03:29 PM||||In case you couldn't tell, that was a joke.||||reg||1
